**How to implement.** S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The mapping table in the kit bar's copy panel (the S7.2 brief; 001 §O 'Automation'; .spec-md §4 'UI'; AGENTS.md: every control of every window can be scrolled fully on screen). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the kit-bar group (steps 188, 226): `kitCopyItemList` (`"KitCopyItemList"`), with a one-line doc. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, beside `kitCopyExperimentToggle` (step 226): `static member kitCopyItemChoice (sourceItem : ItemId) (choice : ItemCopyChoice) : ConstructorUiId` is `KitCopyItemChoice_<the source GUID>_Add` for `AddCopiedItem` and `KitCopyItemChoice_<the source GUID>_<the kit item's GUID>` for `MapOntoKitItem`, with a one-line doc citing spec 0050 S7.2. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs`, the copy panel (step 226): when `src.itemRows` is not empty, the `ScrollViewer` carrying `kitCopyExperimentList` holds, below the experiment toggles, the wrapping line `Items the chosen experiments use: add each to this kit, or use an item it already has.` and a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `kitCopyItemList` of one block per row: the line `<source label> — <row.sourceItem.model.entryReferenceOpt's EntryReference.describe>` (step 213) and a `WrapPanel` of the choices `Add` (`AddCopiedItem`) and `Use <label>` for each item of `model.kitItems` (`MapOntoKitItem` of its id), each carrying `kitCopyItemChoice` and sending `ChooseCopiedItem`, the row's choice an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground` and the others `verbButton`s (the MaterialsWindowView actionButton / verbButton styling already used by the kit bar). The table shares the experiment list's scroller (`MaxHeight` 160), so the bar's tallest height is unchanged and no control leaves the screen. Its doc says so in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2. Tests. `KitWindowTests` (step 184), screens mounted as step 188's: without a trait, `the copy-mapping UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: `kitCopyItemList`'s text and `kitCopyItemChoice` of a test-local source GUID with `AddCopiedItem` and with `MapOntoKitItem` of a second GUID. `an open source lists the items its chosen experiments use, each with Add and the kit's items, the choice marked`: over a model whose `kitCopyOpt` holds a source with Laser600 mapped onto the kit's Laser600 and QZ added, `kitCopyItemList` holds two blocks; Laser600's `Use Laser600` choice and QZ's `Add` are marked; every choice box is inside `kitCopyExperimentList`. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing boxes at their centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` does: `pressing a mapping choice and Copy adds or maps the item as chosen`: over a shell whose `kitPicker` answers a source folder kit holding E1 and the item Laser600 (made as in step 228), pressing `kitCopyExperimentsButton`, E1's toggle, Laser600's `Add` choice and `kitCopyChosenButton` leaves `Laser600 (2).item-json` in the window's kit folder beside its own Laser600's file, and `kitStatus` starting `Copied 1 experiment(s) and added 1 item(s)`. `the kit window: the kit bar and the page stay reachable` (steps 188, 226) keeps its assertion over a copy source whose forty experiments are chosen and whose twenty items each have a row. The `pressing a mapping choice and Copy adds or maps the item as chosen` smoke fact MUST also exercise Use <label> for target T with an id distinct from both source pieces sharing that model. After the button sends ChooseCopiedItem and Copy, close and reopen the target; Experiment.itemsUsedBy MUST resolve the copied experiment to T.id and T.parameters, and the source's unselected piece MUST be absent. The Add branch MUST assert the reopened descriptor retains the added source ItemId. File-count/status assertions alone MUST NOT satisfy either branch.

**Acceptance.** After the mapping buttons dispatch ChooseCopiedItem and Copy, reopening the kit MUST show the copied experiment bound to the chosen target physical id or added source id; mapping controls MUST remain reachable and intent-addressable; constructor-unit-tests, selected ui-tests, ui-smoke, build, elevation and the s22 invariants MUST pass.
